## Control plane boundary (mandatory)

- **Never modify** the Reshapr control plane or the [reshapr](https://github.com/reshaprio/reshapr) backend (`control-plane/`, new Quarkus resources, new REST endpoints, etc.). This workspace is **UI-only**; the contributor does not ship backend changes from here.
- If a feature needs an API that is **not** available on the control plane (or only under `/api/admin/*` without a tenant-safe `/api/v1/*` equivalent), **stop and tell the user** what is missing so they can request it from the Reshapr team. Do not implement backend workarounds on your own initiative.
- In this repo, prefer: client-side aggregation from existing `/api/v1/*` calls, partial UI (`—` + short explanation), or patterns already supported (e.g. MCP prompts via control-plane artifacts). Optional: suggest an upstream issue/PR wording for the user to open on reshapr.

## Quick technical rules

- On-prem auth: `POST /auth/login/reshapr` → token in `sessionStorage`; `Authorization: Bearer` on `/api/v1/*`.
- SaaS: OAuth not implemented in the UI; message on the login screen.
- CORS: `RESHAPR_HTTP_CORS_ORIGINS` on the Quarkus **control plane**; Vite dev origin is often `http://localhost:5173`.
- **Plans** and **secrets** updates: **PUT** (aligned with Quarkus + CLI), not PATCH.

## Language

- **Documentation** in this repository is in **English**.
- When replying to the user, follow the language they use in the conversation.
